0,Ogbronuagum language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ogbronuagum_language,"Language family. Niger–Congo?Ogbronuagum, also called Bukuma after a village in which it is spoken, is a Central Delta language of Nigeria. Ogbronuagum is formed from the two words ""Ogbronu"" and ""Agum"", which would literally mean ""the language of the people of Agum"".",Ogbronuagum,Niger-Congo
1,"Ogbronuagum - Viquipèdia, l'enciclopèdia lliure",https://ca.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ogbronuagum,"L'Ogbronuagum és una llengua que es parla a l'estat de Rivers del sud de Nigèria. Es parla concretament a la LGA de Degema, a la zona de la ciutat de Bukuma.",Ogbronuagum,Niger-Congo
2,Ogbronuagum - ogu (Niger-Congo) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/ogu/,"Ogbronuagum (ogu) is part of the Niger-Congo family and Niger-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Volta-Congo, Benue-Congo, Cross River, Delta Cross, Central Delta class. Ogbronuagum speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts",Ogbronuagum,Niger-Congo
